  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Democratic Governance in Guinea Bissau</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The action aims at strengthening democratic governance in Guinea Bissau, with the purpose of consolidating democracy and facilitating lasting peace in the country. The action will be based on three essential support components: civil society, parliament[1] and elections. The expected results are: (1) strengthened civil society organisations (CSOs) in their role to ensure the vitality of democratic life; (2) trusted and more transparent and accessible democratic institutions at the national level, namely the National Popular Assembly (ANP); (3) smooth electoral cycle processes. The action builds on lessons learned from previous and ongoing EU projects supporting CSOs, the Parliament and electoral processes. The three components of the action, while contributing to the same overall objective, should be implemented with different modalities: indirect management with an entrusted entity or a grant for the CSO component (EUR 3M), a grant to International Institute for Democracy and Electoral Assistance (International IDEA) (EUR 1M), and a top up to the UE contribution to the basket fund for elections (1M) or a grant to International IDEA.[1]Guinea-Bissau is one of the few parliamentary democracies in Africa and, as such, the Parliament plays a key role within the governance system and needs to be supported.</narrative>
  </description>
